# .env and .env.production are NOT excluded, deliberately. They are the second
# channel by which VITE_* reaches `vite build` — see the note at the top of the
# Dockerfile. Everything in them ends up in the browser bundle anyway, so there
# is nothing here to keep out of an image layer; the day a non-VITE_ secret is
# written to one of these files, that stops being true, and this decision has to
# be revisited.
#
# The .local variants are excluded: those are one developer's machine, and a
# laptop's API URL shipping to production is exactly the accident this file
# exists to prevent.
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Rebuilt inside the image. A stale dist/ copied in would be overwritten by
# `npm run build`, but it would also bust the layer cache on every change.
node_modules
dist

.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
*.log
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
